## 2. `wrangler.jsonc` for a DO + Static-Assets worker (2026)

### Keys (all verified)
- `durable_objects.bindings`: array of `{ name, class_name }` (plus optional `script_name` for cross-Worker bindings). ([Use WebSockets — wrangler config](https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/best-practices/websockets/).)
- `migrations`: array of `{ tag, new_sqlite_classes: [...] }` (legacy flow). `new_sqlite_classes` → SQLite backend (required for new namespaces and on Free plan). `new_classes` → legacy KV backend (cannot create new namespaces except for accounts that already have KV-backed ones; **not available on Free plan**). The modern replacement is the `exports` map (`{ "Room": { "type": "durable-object", "storage": "sqlite" } }`), which is mutually exclusive with `migrations`. ([Durable Object class exports](https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/reference/durable-objects-migrations/).)
- `assets` block: `{ directory, binding?, not_found_handling?, run_worker_first? }`.
  - `directory` (required) — folder of static files.
  - `binding` (optional) — name exposed as `env.ASSETS` (`Fetcher`) for `env.ASSETS.fetch(request)`.
  - `not_found_handling` — `"single-page-application"` | `"404-page"` | (omit for default 404).
  - `run_worker_first` — `boolean` or `Array<string>` of glob patterns (e.g. `["/api/*", "!/api/docs/*"]`) to run the Worker before assets for selected paths.
  ([Static Assets — Configuration and Bindings](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/binding/), last updated 2026-04-23; [Static Assets overview](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/), last updated 2026-07-03.)
- `compatibility_date` — a date string (the docs' own 2026 examples use `"2026-07-24"`). `compatibility_flags` is optional and only needed to opt into/out of specific behaviors (e.g. `nodejs_compat`); the WebSocket auto-close behavior is gated by compat date (`>= 2026-04-07`), not a flag you set. ([Compatibility flags](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/compatibility-flags/) referenced from the DO base class page.)

### Full example file (combined DO + assets + custom domain)
This merges the verified DO example config ([websocket-hibernation-server](https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/examples/websocket-hibernation-server/)) with the verified assets block ([static-assets/binding](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/binding/)) and the verified Custom Domain route ([custom-domains](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/routing/custom-domains/)):

```jsonc
{
  "$schema": "./node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "fallguys-game",
  "main": "src/index.ts",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-07-24",
  // Optional; add only if you need Node.js built-ins:
  // "compatibility_flags": ["nodejs_compat"],

  "assets": {
    "directory": "./public/",
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    "not_found_handling": "single-page-application",
    // Run the Worker (Hono) first for game/API paths, assets-first otherwise:
    "run_worker_first": ["/api/*", "/ws/*", "!/api/docs/*"]
  },

  "durable_objects": {
    "bindings": [
      { "name": "ROOMS", "class_name": "Room" }
    ]
  },

  // Legacy migrations flow (still supported). Modern alternative: use "exports"
  // instead of "migrations" — they are mutually exclusive.
  "migrations": [
    { "tag": "v1", "new_sqlite_classes": ["Room"] }
  ],

  // Custom Domain (see §4). Deploy with `wrangler deploy`:
  "routes": [
    { "pattern": "game.example.com", "custom_domain": true }
  ],

  "observability": { "enabled": true }
}
```

> The `exports` alternative (newer, recommended for greenfield projects) would replace the `migrations` block with:
> ```jsonc
> "exports": { "Room": { "type": "durable-object", "storage": "sqlite" } }
> ```
> ([Durable Object class exports — Define a class](https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/reference/durable-objects-migrations/#define-a-durable-object-class).)

