## 4. Custom Domain deployment

Source: [Custom Domains](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/routing/custom-domains/) (last updated 2026-06-23).

- **Wrangler config vs dashboard.** You can attach a Custom Domain either in the dashboard (**Workers & Pages → *Worker* → Settings → Domains & Routes → Add → Custom Domain**) or in `wrangler.jsonc` by adding `custom_domain: true` to a `routes` entry:
  ```jsonc
  {
    "routes": [
      { "pattern": "game.example.com", "custom_domain": true }
    ]
  }
  ```
  Deploy with `npx wrangler deploy`. (Same page, "Set up a Custom Domain in your Wrangler configuration file".)
- **DNS records Cloudflare creates automatically.** "After you set up a Custom Domain for your Worker, Cloudflare will create DNS records and issue necessary certificates on your behalf. The created DNS records will point directly to your Worker." It also generates an **Advanced Certificate**. (Same page, "Background" / "Certificates".)
- **Requirements.** You need (1) an active Cloudflare zone and (2) a Worker. The zone must be one you own on the same Cloudflare account as the Worker (you "cannot create a Custom Domain on a hostname with an existing CNAME DNS record or on a zone you do not own"). (Same page, "Add a Custom Domain".)
- **Subdomain like `game.example.com`.** Put the exact hostname in `pattern`. Custom Domains require an **exact hostname match** (path/query are ignored); wildcard DNS is **not** supported. To support both `example.com` and `game.example.com`, add each as a separate Custom Domain route. (Same page, "Request matching behaviour".)
- **Gotchas / errors people hit:**
  - Existing CNAME on the hostname blocks creation — delete the conflicting DNS record first. (Same page, "Caution".)
  - `example.com` vs `www.example.com` are distinct exact matches; to redirect one to the other you need a redirect rule **plus** a proxied placeholder DNS record (`A 192.0.2.0` or `AAAA 100::`) on the source hostname. (Same page, "Redirect between www and root domain".)
  - Deleting a Custom Domain does **not** auto-delete the Advanced Certificate — remove it manually. (Same page, "Certificates".)
  - Same-zone Worker→Worker `fetch()` only works without a service binding when the target is on a **Custom Domain** (not a route). (Same page, "Worker to Worker communication".)

