## 6. Testing DO WebSockets

### Local manual testing: `wrangler dev`
Both the [websocket-hibernation-server example](https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/examples/websocket-hibernation-server/) and the [Hono Cloudflare Workers guide](https://hono.dev/docs/getting-started/cloudflare-workers#_3-run) use `npm run dev` (→ `wrangler dev`) and connect to `http://localhost:8787`. Caveat per §1: under `wrangler dev` the DO is not actually evicted, so hibernation itself isn't exercised locally (events still deliver). ([Use WebSockets — Local development support](https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/best-practices/websockets/).)

### Automated tests: `@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers`
Source: [Testing Durable Objects](https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/examples/testing-with-durable-objects/) (last updated 2026-06-29) and [Vitest integration — Configuration](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/testing/vitest-integration/configuration/) (last updated 2026-07-05). Hono also recommends `@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers`. ([Hono — Cloudflare Workers: Testing](https://hono.dev/docs/getting-started/cloudflare-workers#testing).)

Install (Vitest 4 is the current line):
```sh
npm i -D vitest@^4.1.0 @cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers
```

`vitest.config.ts`:
```ts
import { cloudflareTest } from "@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers";
import { defineConfig } from "vitest/config";

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [
    cloudflareTest({ wrangler: { configPath: "./wrangler.jsonc" } }),
  ],
});
```

`wrangler.jsonc` for tests (the docs use the legacy `migrations` form alongside the vitest config):
```jsonc
{
  "compatibility_date": "2026-07-24",
  "durable_objects": { "bindings": [{ "name": "ROOMS", "class_name": "Room" }] },
  "migrations": [{ "tag": "v1", "new_sqlite_classes": ["Room"] }]
}
```

Test APIs available from `cloudflare:workers` / `cloudflare:test`:
- `env` from `cloudflare:workers` → `env.ROOMS.idFromName(...)` / `env.ROOMS.get(id)` for direct RPC.
- `exports.default.fetch(...)` for HTTP/integration tests through the Worker.
- `runInDurableObject(stub, async (instance, state) => {...})` — inspect internals/storage.
- `runDurableObjectAlarm(stub)` — fire the alarm immediately (returns `true` if one was scheduled).
- `evictDurableObject(stub, options?)` — evict an instance; `options.webSockets` is `"hibernate"` (default) or `"close"`. The docs' example accepts a WebSocket via `stub.fetch("https://example.com", { headers: { Upgrade: "websocket" } })`, then `response.webSocket.accept()`, evicts, and asserts messages still round-trip. ([Testing Durable Objects — Testing WebSocket behavior across eviction](https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/examples/testing-with-durable-objects/#testing-websocket-behavior-across-eviction).)
- `listDurableObjectIds(namespace)`, `evictAllDurableObjects()`.

Example WebSocket-eviction test (verbatim shape from the docs):
```ts
import { env } from "cloudflare:workers";
import { evictDurableObject } from "cloudflare:test";
import { describe, it, expect } from "vitest";

describe("Room WebSocket eviction", () => {
  it("hibernates WebSockets across eviction by default", async () => {
    const id = env.ROOMS.idFromName("ws-test");
    const stub = env.ROOMS.get(id);

    const res = await stub.fetch("https://example.com", {
      headers: { Upgrade: "websocket" },
    });
    const socket = res.webSocket;
    if (!socket) throw new Error("Expected WebSocket response");
    socket.accept();

    await evictDurableObject(stub); // hibernates by default

    const msg = new Promise<string>((resolve) =>
      socket.addEventListener("message", (e) => resolve(e.data as string))
    );
    socket.send("after-eviction");
    expect(await msg).toBe("after-eviction");
    socket.close(1000, "done");
  });
});
```

A runnable DO + Vitest fixture is in the workers-sdk repo: [`fixtures/vitest-pool-workers-examples/durable-objects` @ `6e0bf6e`](https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/tree/6e0bf6e917bf4a2b9cd3ee741e625174075e38e1/fixtures/vitest-pool-workers-examples/durable-objects).

For a Hono app specifically, Hono's own `app.request(url)` works in plain Vitest (no Workers runtime) for handler logic, but to exercise real DO bindings/WebSockets you use `@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers` as above (Hono explicitly recommends it). ([Hono — Cloudflare Workers: Testing](https://hono.dev/docs/getting-started/cloudflare-workers#testing).)

